Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ak7375: wait for AK7377 active mode before DAC restore

Apollo's immutable AK7377 module definition requests a 1000us delay after
register2=0. The driver waits before the mode write but immediately restores
the DAC afterwards. A filtered native trace on kernel18 captured mode02-00
ACK followed by position00-00-00 NACK only104us after the mode request, with
no controller suspend between them. Earlier power-delay tests did not cover
this distinct active-mode settling interval.

Add a per-chip interval, set only for AK7377, before the first restore write.
Keep other chips, rail routing, pre-power delay and error propagation intact.
No retries, PM-error clears, calibration or firmware writes are introduced.
The native baseline motivates testing; optical focus is not thereby proven.

---

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ak7375.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ak7375.c
@@ -36,6 +36,8 @@
 	 * I2C messages.
 	 */
 	u16 power_delay_us;
+	/* Active-mode settling before the first position command. */
+	u16 mode_active_delay_us;
 };
 
 static const struct ak73xx_chipdef ak7345_cdef = {
@@ -78,6 +80,7 @@
 	.ctrl_steps = 64,
 	.ctrl_delay_us = 1000,
 	.power_delay_us = 10000,
+	.mode_active_delay_us = 1000,
 };
 
 static const char * const ak7375_supply_names[] = {
@@ -327,6 +330,11 @@
 		goto disable_supplies;
 	}
 
+	/* The AK7377 needs a settling interval after leaving standby. */
+	if (cdef->mode_active_delay_us)
+		usleep_range(cdef->mode_active_delay_us,
+			     cdef->mode_active_delay_us + 100);
+
 	for (val = ak7375_dev->focus->val % cdef->ctrl_steps;
 	     val <= ak7375_dev->focus->val;
 	     val += cdef->ctrl_steps) {
